{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1473326-drivethru-pod-service","id":1473326,"title":"DriveThru POD service...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-26T02:55:16-08:00","id":1473326,"title":"DriveThru POD service...","content":"I understand that this may not be the proper channel to report this but I think someone at Onyx Path needs to know at least some of the treatment that print on demand customers are getting from DriveThru RPG. The below post that I have also submitted to DriveThru RPGs discussion section under the Chronicles of Darkness page should explain everything:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Okay I ordered this book (Chronicles of Darkness main book POD) on the 30th of December in standard print format. I also ordered 3 other Chronicles of Darkness books, I have received all of the other books much faster than I thought I would have but by the 12th of January I still had not received this book and looking at the USPS tracking information it stated: &quot;Label Created, not yet in system.&quot; To this day the 26th of January it still reads the same thing when I enter the tracking number. On the 12th of January I was told that the printer could not verify that the order had shipped, Oh and yes I submitted a ticket and spoke to people on numerous occasions about this, I was told that a new order had been sent to the printer and that I would be notified when it shipped. Days went by and nothing, more days went by and nothing and I was asking them about the shipment through all this time, they told me that when the order was shipped that I would receive an updated tracking number in place of the one on the old order, still nothing. It is now</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the 26th of January the order has had time to have been delivered to me at least three times over and I have still heard nothing, and every time somebody replies to my ticket they have the audacity to mark it as solved. I send another statement to them and it comes up unsolved again they send a correspondence back and it's marked solved again which it is clearly not solved until I say it is solved by verifying that I have received the book. Oh and the order says that it was shipped on the 29th of January which is a day before I placed the order. They did give me a $10 store credit to use and I am thankful for that but I have paid for what basically amounts to a $50 book and I have received a $10 gift certificate. I went to complain again on the same ticket and it's marked solved again and it's been closed for comments forcing me to submit a follow up ticket in order to pursue it any further. Has anyone experienced service this poor on a print item from DriveThru RPG before? These books were the first POD titles that I have ever ordered through DriveThru and the books that I have received have all been fine quality but they have to finish the job. Folks you can't have a guy order 4 books and successfully send 3 of them and say 3 out of 4 ain't bad. I am not going to shut up until this is resolved. I am posting this here so that DriveThru knows that the pressure is being applied and that I am going to spread this bad press until they do something about it. Will I ever order print on demand from here again? I would have to say if there was another option at this point I probably would not. The other three books are fine but you have to do a complete job.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Is there another option besides DriveThru RPG to buy Onyx Path books? Does anyone know of one? After this experience I am not sure that I want to order POD from them again. There needs to be some competition in this RPG POD market in order to keep these guys on their toes. If anyone from Onyx Path would like to get in touch with me over this my email is <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#09737e707d383b3a496e64686065276a6664\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"176d606e6326252457707a767e7b3974787a\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> I can provide proof of purchase receipts or whatever. If there is another place that I should have sent this message to someone please direct me to it. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Charles</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt","name":"Zwyt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T06:03:05-08:00","id":1473569,"title":"","content":"The short answer is that there is no other option. The RPG industry is incredible tiny, and honestly the fact that there is a dedicated, brand-agnostic PoD producer at all is a bit remarkable.<br /> <br /> You can sometimes find PoD books being sold second hand. Amazon and ebay are two obvious places to check, and <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nobleknight.com</a> often has good supplies. You can also sometimes find stock from the kickstarted books, which tend to be higher quality than the PoD variants, though the CofD core never had a kickstarter.<br /> <br /> I would also encourage reaching out to DriveThru again. Although there's no excuse for leaving you out in the cold like this, I would say that my experiences with them have been very positive for the most part. I also know that they have been facing tremendous difficulty during the pandemic (along with the rest of the RPG industry) as both the costs of PoD have been going up and the costs and also the reliability of shipping have been getting much worse. OPP's own kickstarter projects have seen the printed books delayed by 6 months or more to give you some context for how bad the situation is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}